Rerolling until you get a ring of levitation doesn't teach you how to
play without levitation. Rerolling until you get a ring of slow
digestion doesn't teach you how to deal with hunger during play. These
are the precise examples that began this stupid subthread.

Starting *stats* have very little effect on the subsequent game.
Starting *equipment* only has a significant effect if the player
doesn't know how to deal with a particular obstacle that the game
presents. Playing only characters that compensate for a player's
innate playing deficiencies does not help a player overcome these
deficiencies. This should be obvious.

On a more positive note, I'm glad you expressed appreciation for Mikko
Saari's Beginner's Guide. I too think it's a great help.

